Just an update - I now have set up a somewhat naive way to sync bones files=
.

I modified Vulture's launch script to:
1) Start Unison (http://www.cis.upenn.edu/~bcpierce/unison/) in the backgro=
und, syncing the playground  with a Unison daemon on the server every 5 sec=
onds while the game is running (Unison has its own repeat command).
2) Do one last sync after the game shuts down to grab bones from dying.

It ultimately ended up being less work, in terms of script code written, to=
 do the bones syncing than the scores.  Most of the time I spent was just d=
ealing with Unison's esoteric config syntax, as well as learning how to com=
pile NetHack for the first time in order to adjust some options for bones c=
ompatibility.

Limitations:
1) Connection failures will deprive the server from knowing about new bones=
, or hearing about consumptions.
One idea is to treat this condition like a disconnect when playing text-sty=
le over ssh/telnet, only a little more gracefully since the game doesn't ne=
ed to stop.  The player could be prompted to choose to continue playing and=
 sacrifice the ability to consume/produce bones until the connection is res=
tored, or save and go fix the issue.
2) There is a very small chance that 2 players arriving on the same bones l=
evel within the sync interval could both consume a bones file.
The game could be modded to sync only right before it checks for bones for =
a level, or after death.


